2. **Tangents from a Point to a Parabola:**
   The tangent to a parabola at a point \( (x_0, y_0) \) is given by the equation \( yy_0 = 2a(x - x_0) \). For our parabola \( y^2 = 8x \), the tangent at \( (x_0, y_0) \) is \( yy_0 = 2 \cdot 2(x - x_0) \), which simplifies to \( yy_0 = 4(x - x_0) \).

